+# Adapter r1.4 — offline A4 deltas from r1.3
+
+A4 changes only the dedicated key ceiling/label and their pinned authority.
+KEY_LABEL is `DocketClock`; KEY_MAX is 50_000_000_000 nanoUSD ($50.00).
+Non-resetting limit and zero initial usage are still mandatory. The actual R17
+plan is three OPQ calls; synthetic six-call tests remain regression coverage.
+
+The import now checks recon-a4/READY.json and loads recon-a4/r17recon.py with
+SHA-256 `8c98fabdc73fad10336698fa695869966a631d5a7d99b797725f2c711b1b6bb0`.
+Release recon artifacts are separately hash-pinned rather than required inside
+the frozen design directory. Original design artifacts retain their original
+freeze; the amended recon must be the release recon and INIT recon pin.
+The native shim resolves adapter-r1-4/host_driver.py.
+
+FLOOR $0.27, OPERATING $1.80, CAP $2.00, all-remaining-call reservations,
+admission, reconciliation, debit, anomaly halts, no-retry and A3 timeouts stay
+unchanged. The provider ceiling no longer backstops CAP; the accepted residual
+risk in A4 remains. No live evidence or release approval is synthesized here.
+
+Original L01–L25 tests run frozen check.py with its ORIGINAL engine. The new
+A4 comparison runs the same 25 unchanged cases against recon-a4: ONLY
+L18-key-limit-bounds changes ($1.74 / six calls: False -> True). Its result
+vector is [True, True, True, False] versus [True, False, True, False]. L12
+retains its HALT outcome (its explicit original limit is also a mismatch now).
+
+Ten A4 tests cover three successful synthetic OPQ calls at $50/usage zero,
+above-$50/resetting/nonzero-usage/wrong-label refusals, attestation/machine
+refusals, independent OPERATING bounds (including seventh FLOOR and reserving
+all remaining calls), and the exact L-fixture outcome comparison. Together
+with the inherited 190 tests, 200 adapter tests run per interpreter. Monetary
+precision parser examples retaining $1.73 are intentional historical inputs.
+
+Commands: `R17_TEST_PYTHON=<python> sh adapter-r1-4/run_tests.sh`; all Python
+scripts use `-I -S -B`. Both required interpreters are recorded in READY.json.
+Logs under _out are excluded from payload pins; suite outputs have their own
+recorded hashes. verify_ready.py reruns all three folders' suites and verifies
+every inventory/dependency/READY pin and the frozen inputs afterward.
+
+All edits are confined to adapter-r1-4, recon-a4 and release-prep-a4. No network,
+provider, executor, runner, release, signing or credential operation was run.
+No actual parsed source body or reference content was read. Repro subprocesses
+use synthetic transports/evidence and remain offline. Independent primary
+review, normalized live evidence and staging/signing remain outstanding.
+
+---
+
